{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These, etc.</b> All the commentators agreed in their opinion that the section beginning 'Behold, YHWH will empty the earth' refers to the future, to the war of Gog and Magog, and according to the opinion of Rabbi Moses the Kohen it speaks of the king of Assyria, and 'the feast of rich food' (Isaiah 25:6) concerns the death of the camp of Sennacherib and his hosts; 'the crown of pride' (Isaiah 28:1):" "<b>These.</b> The escapees." "<b>They shall sing.</b> Raising the voice, and from the verse 'and the song passed by' (1 Kings 22:36). <b>Waters.</b> Those who go by sea; likewise the word 'prance' [in 'prance, O inhabitants'] — and the proof is 'the horse prances'."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:00.007402635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}